@startuml
title Duration refresh: evidence to reviewed history
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
left to right direction
rectangle "CI collects one cohort\nProject + suite + revision\nKeep shard directories" as ci
rectangle "Existing TEST-*.xml\nEligibility baseline / bytecode\nImmutable previous TSV" as inputs
rectangle "Gradle refresh task\nor Maven standalone goal\nNo producer dependencies" as adapter
rectangle "Shared core\nSecure XML metadata\nComplete class families\nPrune, merge, floor, round" as core
rectangle "Candidate durations.tsv\ndurations.json: PASSED" as success
rectangle "durations.json: FAILED\nRemove stale candidate TSV\nFail task / goal" as failure
rectangle "Human review\nAdopt in a later commit\nNext pipeline uses one snapshot" as review
ci --> inputs
inputs --> adapter
adapter --> core
core --> success : Accepted evidence
core --> failure : Invalid / insufficient data
success --> review
note bottom of adapter
  Invalid configuration: reject before parsing.
  I/O errors fail the build; writes are not atomic.
end note
note bottom of review
  Keep native test and selection-coverage gates.
  Recorded loads are not wall-clock predictions.
  Refresh never overwrites maintained history.
end note
@enduml
